{
  "id": "professional-licensing",
  "term": "professional licensing",
  "definition": "Professional licensing is the formal process of assessing whether someone meets the knowledge standards required for entry into a profession, often through a licensing examination. Passing such an exam shows performance on codified knowledge but does not by itself demonstrate full clinical judgment or readiness for independent practice.",
