      "reasons": [
        "The packet only discusses licensing examinations in the context of nursing and does not support the general claim that professional licensing is “the formal process of assessing whether someone meets the knowledge standards required for entry into a profession” (or that this is “often” done via licensing examinations).",
        "While the packet supports the idea that exam performance reflects codified knowledge (e.g., codified nursing knowledge reaching approximate passing thresholds) and that such performance does not demonstrate clinical readiness/independent practice, the definition’s first sentence contains additional general process claims that are not evidenced in the packet."
